<?xml version="1.0" standalone="yes"?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name "thevault.login">
<!ENTITY author "Asuka">
<!ENTITY version "2026.10.19g">
<!ENTITY plugdir "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gunner007cd/thevault-login/main/thevault.login.plg">
<!ENTITY support "https://github.com/gunner007cd/thevault-login">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;"
        author="&author;"
        version="&version;"
        pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
        support="&support;"
        min="7.3.2"
        icon="lock">
<CHANGES>
###2026.10.19g
- Added a stable GitHub pluginURL so Unraid can check for updates normally.
- Added the project repository as the support link.
- No functional login or authentication changes from 2026.10.19f.

###2026.10.19f
- Simplified author credit to Asuka.
- Removed the extra designer-credit line from the Plugin Manager description.
- No functional login or authentication changes from 2026.10.19e.

###2026.10.19e
- Fixed Plugin Manager presentation: README is now created by the installer after the plugin directory exists.
- Installed Plugins now shows the friendly "TheVault Login" name and description instead of falling back to the internal ID.
- Removed unused Title/DESCRIPTION manifest fields; current Unraid Plugin Manager uses README.md for the visible description.
- Functional login theme is unchanged from 2026.10.19d.

###2026.10.19d
- Added friendly Plugin Manager title: TheVault Login.
- Added plugin description and login-themed icon.
- Updated author credit to Asuka / TheVault.
- No functional login/authentication changes from 2026.10.19c.

###2026.10.19c
- Replaced the CSS pseudo-element version footer with a real HTML footer element.
- Version footer is inserted directly below Password Recovery.
- Keeps the fully inline pre-auth-safe CSS/background architecture from 2026.10.19b.
- Cleans up earlier external hooks, inline test blocks, and repeated installs idempotently.

###2026.10.19b
- Switched the login theme to a fully inline pre-auth-safe design.
- Background image is embedded directly into the login page as a WebP data URI.
- Added a muted dynamic Unraid version footer read from /etc/unraid-version.
- Removes the older external stylesheet hook automatically when upgrading.

###2026.10.19a
- Initial TheVault login-only split theme.
</CHANGES>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
#!/bin/bash
set -eu

NAME="thevault.login"
VERSION="2026.10.19g"
PLUGDIR="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/$NAME"
PRIMARY="/usr/local/emhttp/webGui/include/.login.php"
MIRROR="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/dynamix/include/.login.php"

mkdir -p "$PLUGDIR"

# Plugin Manager renders this README as the friendly plugin name/description.
cat > "$PLUGDIR/README.md" <<'EOF_THEVAULT_README'
**TheVault Login**

A login-only visual customization for TheVault's Unraid sign-in page. It keeps Unraid's native authentication, sessions, SSO, rate limiting, and password recovery untouched while presenting the stock login form as a responsive split-screen layout with locally embedded homelab artwork and a subtle running Unraid version footer.

EOF_THEVAULT_README
chmod 0644 "$PLUGDIR/README.md"

cat > "$PLUGDIR/login.css" <<'EOF_THEVAULT_LOGIN_CSS'
/* TheVault Login - login-page-only styling for Unraid 7.3.2 */
:root {
    --tv-login-panel: min(620px, max(430px, 38vw));
    --tv-bg: #090e14;
    --tv-panel-bg: rgba(11, 16, 22, 0.97);
    --tv-line: #34404c;
    --tv-muted: #98a5b3;
}

html,
body {
    min-height: 100%;
}

body {
    min-height: 100vh !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
    overflow: hidden !important;
    background: var(--tv-bg) !important;
}

/* Static image panel. No markup changes required. */
body::before {
    content: "";
    position: fixed;
    z-index: 0;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    left: var(--tv-login-panel);
    background-image:
        linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(9, 14, 20, 0.40) 0%, rgba(9, 14, 20, 0.10) 18%, rgba(9, 14, 20, 0) 42%),
        url('__THEVAULT_BACKGROUND__');
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center center;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    pointer-events: none;
}

/* Turn the existing Unraid login card into the full-height left panel. */
#login {
    position: relative !important;
    z-index: 1 !important;
    box-sizing: border-box !important;
    width: var(--tv-login-panel) !important;
    max-width: none !important;
    min-height: 100vh !important;
    height: 100vh !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
    border-radius: 0 !important;
    overflow-y: auto !important;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(14, 20, 27, 0.985), var(--tv-panel-bg)) !important;
    box-shadow: 24px 0 70px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.48) !important;
    display: flex !important;
    flex-direction: column !important;
    justify-content: center !important;
}

#login::after {
    display: none !important;
}

#login .logo {
    flex: 0 0 auto !important;
    height: 108px !important;
    border-radius: 0 !important;
    background: transparent !important;
    margin: 0 auto !important;
    width: min(390px, calc(100% - 72px)) !important;
}

#login .logo::before,
#login .logo::after,
#login .angle::before,
#login .angle::after {
    display: none !important;
}

#login .wordmark {
    display: flex !important;
    align-items: center !important;
    height: 100% !important;
    padding: 0 !important;
}

#login .wordmark svg {
    width: 190px !important;
    height: auto !important;
    max-height: 54px !important;
}

#login .content {
    box-sizing: border-box !important;
    width: min(390px, calc(100% - 72px)) !important;
    margin: 0 auto !important;
    padding: 8px 0 44px !important;
    float: none !important;
}

#login h1 {
    margin: 0 0 5px !important;
    color: #ffffff !important;
    font-size: 1.85rem !important;
    font-weight: 600 !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em !important;
}

#login h2 {
    margin: 0 0 32px !important;
    color: var(--tv-muted) !important;
    font-size: 0.88rem !important;
    font-weight: 400 !important;
    line-height: 1.45 !important;
}

/* The server case art is nice on the stock card, but fights this layout. */
#login .case {
    display: none !important;
}

#login .form,
#login .form form,
#login .form p {
    width: 100% !important;
    box-sizing: border-box !important;
}

#login input[type='text'],
#login input[type='password'] {
    box-sizing: border-box !important;
    width: 100% !important;
    margin: 0 0 14px !important;
    padding: 13px 14px !important;
    border: 1px solid var(--tv-line) !important;
    border-radius: 4px !important;
    background: #111821 !important;
    color: #ffffff !important;
    box-shadow: none !important;
}

#login input[type='text']::placeholder,
#login input[type='password']::placeholder {
    color: #7f8b98 !important;
    opacity: 1 !important;
}

#login input[type='text']:focus,
#login input[type='password']:focus {
    border-color: #ff8c2f !important;
    outline: none !important;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 140, 47, 0.18) !important;
}

#login .button,
#login .button--small {
    box-sizing: border-box !important;
    width: 100% !important;
    margin: 2px 0 6px !important;
    padding: 13px 18px !important;
}

#login a {
    color: #ff8c2f !important;
}


/* Small build footer, inserted as real HTML below Password Recovery. */
#thevault-login-version {
    margin-top: 14px;
    color: #66727f;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
}

#login .error {
    line-height: 1.45 !important;
}

@media (max-width: 900px) {
    :root {
        --tv-login-panel: 100vw;
    }

    body {
        overflow: auto !important;
    }

    body::before {
        display: none !important;
    }

    #login {
        width: 100vw !important;
        min-height: 100vh !important;
        height: auto !important;
        box-shadow: none !important;
    }

    #login .logo,
    #login .content {
        width: min(390px, calc(100% - 44px)) !important;
    }
}
EOF_THEVAULT_LOGIN_CSS

cat <<'EOF_THEVAULT_LOGIN_IMAGE' | base64 -d > "$PLUGDIR/background.webp"
